From: Ferrite overlay
Subject: [PATCH] std.heap: default page_size_min for riscv freestanding

Zig's `page_size_min_default` table omits riscv32/riscv64 from the
`.freestanding`/`.other` branch, so `std.heap.page_size_min` hits a
`@compileError` for `riscv64-freestanding`. This breaks any std code
that references it, e.g. `std.Io.File.MemoryMap` (pulled in via
`std.http` in wget), even though it compiles fine on aarch64 and
x86_64 freestanding which the table already covers.

riscv uses 4 KiB base pages on every real OS entry in this same table
(Linux/FreeBSD/NetBSD/...), so default freestanding riscv to 4 KiB to
match aarch64/x86_64. page_size_max is unaffected: MemoryMap only
references page_size_min, which is why aarch64 (also without a
freestanding page_size_max default) already builds.

--- a/std/heap.zig
+++ b/std/heap.zig
@@ -840,6 +840,7 @@
         .wasm32, .wasm64 => 64 << 10,
         .x86, .x86_64 => 4 << 10,
         .aarch64, .aarch64_be => 4 << 10,
+        .riscv32, .riscv64 => 4 << 10,
         else => null,
     },
     else => null,
